# automation-testing settings
# Copy to .env (`make setup` does it for you), then fill in what you need.
# Exported shell variables always win over this file. Never commit .env.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Where the TopAuto repos are
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Folder that holds the sibling repos. Default: the parent of this repo, i.e.
#   workspace/
#     automation-testing/        <- this repo
#     topautokh-api/             <- backend
#     top-auto-1653-admin-page/  <- Angular admin
# WORKSPACE_ROOT=..
# Override one repo if it lives elsewhere (relative paths resolve against WORKSPACE_ROOT):
# BACKEND_WORKSPACE=topautokh-api
# ADMIN_WORKSPACE=top-auto-1653-admin-page

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Where the running stack is (you start it in your own terminals)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
API_HEALTH_ENDPOINT=/health
# Admin UI used by the Playwright specs in orchestration/ui_tests
BASE_URL=http://localhost:4200
API_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Local MongoDB (replica set). Used by preflight and fixtures/test-identities.js
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/topauto1653_ecommerce?replicaSet=rs0
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/topauto1653_ecommerce?replicaSet=rs0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Auth for the API / security pillars
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JWT_SECRET must match the backend's. Leave it empty to read it from the
# backend repo's own .env at run time (it is never printed).
JWT_SECRET=

# Test identities: run `node fixtures/test-identities.js --apply` and paste its output here.
# BASIC tenant: when empty, the engine uses the "Top Auto Default" company and admin
# employee ids of the team's dev database, which won't exist in a fresh database.
TEST_BASIC_COMPANY_ID=
TEST_BASIC_EMPLOYEE_ID=
TEST_PREMIUM_COMPANY_ID=
TEST_PREMIUM_EMPLOYEE_ID=
TEST_PLATFORM_COMPANY_ID=
TEST_PLATFORM_ADMIN_ID=
# Optional: log in for real instead of minting a JWT
TEST_PREMIUM_PHONE=
TEST_PREMIUM_PASSWORD=
TEST_ADMIN_PHONE=
TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Playwright UI specs log in with this account (needs at least one company)
TEST_PHONE=
TEST_PASSWORD=

# Seconds the API runner may wait out the backend rate limiter (default 920)
# RATE_LIMIT_MAX_WAIT=920

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Where results go
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test runs, evidence and audit logs. Default: ./results (gitignored).
# RESULTS_DIR=results

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Optional tools
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UI pillar command. {ADMIN_WORKSPACE} and {WORKSPACE_ROOT} are substituted.
# Default (orchestration/config.json): npm --prefix "{ADMIN_WORKSPACE}" run test:ci
# UI_TEST_COMMAND=
# ENABLE_ANGULAR_HEADLESS_TEST=true
# JMeter: found on PATH by default
# JMETER_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/jmeter
# JMETER_TEST_PLAN=orchestration/performance/smoke_test.jmx
# Dashboard port (make dashboard)
# DASHBOARD_PORT=8470

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Optional AI (Master Agent `run` command only; the test engine works without it)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
